+# Desktop inspection 1.3.0 (engine 1.2.0)
+
+This source candidate has not been released as a Windows installer. The public
+1.2.0 installer and download site remain unchanged.
+
+## File contents and validation scope
+
+Desktop metadata comes from the same bounded, immutable S0 byte snapshot as the
+report hashes. There is no second read after scanning. Standalone plain text,
+media and document content cannot receive SAFE as a validated GTA mod. Plain
+text inside a supported archive remains analysable context; a README does not
+by itself block a complete supported package. Malicious or suspicious evidence
+still takes precedence over unsupported or damaged formats.
+
+Common WAVE, MPEG, ID3, FLAC, Ogg, ISO media, PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP and PDF headers
+are recognized independently of filename extensions. Header recognition does
+not fully validate a media/document container. A file named `example.asi` whose
+bytes are plain text gets a specific content/extension explanation, file size,
+SHA-256 and a bounded redacted text preview. UTF-8/UTF-16 prefix boundaries are
+handled without mistaking a split character for binary content. Previews use
+at most 8192 captured bytes and display at most 320 characters before redaction.
+Redaction happens before display truncation, including short assigned secrets.
+They are samples, not the complete file contents. Scripts and configuration
+analysis retain the existing conservative static pipeline.
+
+The public immutable Report schema and verdict precedence are retained. Root
+formats outside direct validation mark S0 partial with UNSUPPORTED_FORMAT.
+`Scanner.file_inspection` is supplementary desktop metadata, not a new public
+security verdict. INVALID/INCONCLUSIVE results show an unknown gauge, with no
+needle at zero. Other results display the engine's actual 0–100 evidence score.
+The score and confidence are engineering indicators, not measured probabilities.
+
+## Actual progress and report card
+
+The desktop CLI emits only fixed stage identifiers on stderr; stdout remains
+one JSON result. Stages are announced immediately before the corresponding
+operation. Required isolated parsers, shared ledgers and source-only analysis
+are unchanged. Child analysis is represented by the active archive stage,
+without a simulated percentage or timer that invents progress.
+
+The native bridge reads bounded telemetry, accepts a fixed allowlist of stages
+and sends events only to the main window. A per-scan identifier makes the UI
+ignore delayed events from earlier scans. File selection and scanning serialize
+through the native busy guard. New selections clear previous native reports.
+
+The scan rectangle morphs into a circle with a rotating light, then expands
+into the result. A flip reveals a report card with type, size, explanation,
+hash, preview, evidence, coverage and signed-data details. English remains the
+default, Persian uses RTL, hidden card faces are inert, and reduced motion is
+supported. All sample text is inserted with textContent or drawn on Canvas.
+
+PNG export is generated locally (1200px wide, at most 2600px high); it includes
+summary evidence and the static-analysis limitation. The JSON export carries
+all evidence. Native export accepts bounded PNG bytes and writes a newly chosen
+file with create_new; it cannot accept a sample path or overwrite an input.
+
+## Signed threat updates
+
+The online cache is authenticated using the pinned Ed25519 key; payload hashes,
+record schemas and rule compilation are checked. Status now exposes the signed
+creation time and key identifier, as well as available/fresh/count/version.
+An updater launch is a request, not proof of successful download. A status check
+authenticates the current cache, which may still be the previous good version.
+
+Scheduled updates use the Windows local clock at 03:00. The IExpress installer
+sets StartWhenAvailable, so a missed task can run later subject to Windows task
+conditions; it does not wake a powered-off machine. The legacy NSIS daily task
+does not configure that catch-up setting. Manual updates use UAC because only
+administrators/SYSTEM can write the protected update cache. The trusted updater
+receives no selected sample path. Updates supply hashes/rules, not an app upgrade.
+
+The feed verified on 2026-10-07 contained 1342 unique SHA-256 records, signed at
+2026-10-07T10:37:16.216051+00:00, version mb-37608574476001. This is the published
+feed's count, not confirmation of any user's local cache or a complete malware
+catalogue. No malware sample was downloaded. An exact-hash reputation lookup
+was verified to retain its hard malicious override.
+
+## Reproduce validation
+
+Install the locked Python graph and package before testing; installed subprocess
+checks deliberately do not import from an untrusted working directory:
+
+```sh
+python -m pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-lock.txt
+python -m pip install --no-deps --no-build-isolation .
+python -m pytest -q
+python -m ruff check .
+python -m mypy malguard_core malguard_cli
+cargo check --locked --manifest-path desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml
+```
+
+`cargo check` needs real platform development libraries and the resource directory
+normally supplied by the frozen-engine build. A check-only resource directory
+contains no executable engine and is excluded from source packaging. This check
+is not an installer or native Windows runtime test.
+
+Browser QA uses an actual installed Python scanner and Chromium, substituting
+only the native file picker, IPC transport, protected cache location and save
+dialog. Supply an existing hash-locked Playwright installation, a verified feed
+and an output directory outside the packaged source:
+
+```sh
+PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE=/absolute/path/to/playwright/index.mjs \
+MALGUARD_PYTHON=/absolute/path/to/venv/bin/python \
+MALGUARD_QA_FEED=/absolute/path/to/latest.json \
+MALGUARD_QA_OUTPUT=/tmp/malguard-desktop-qa \
+node tests/desktop/browser.mjs
+```
+
+The test prevents external browser requests and uses harmless generated content.
+The live feed download is a separate read-only verification. Native Windows
+installation, UAC, Task Scheduler, WebView2 event permissions and PNG save dialogs
+must still pass Windows CI/manual testing before publication. Detection accuracy
+against a representative real malware/benign corpus has not been measured.
+
+The previously reported slow Windows download/installation is still an open
+separate issue; this change does not claim to fix it.
